  "answer": "To reduce the risk of an image classifier being tricked by small, deliberate changes (known as adversarial examples), a highly effective proposed defense is \"adversarial training.\" This mechanism works by generating adversarial examples and incorporating them as training samples, allowing the AI model to learn to be robust against them during testing (https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.03824). Other proposed mechanisms include minimizing the effects of small perturbations on the model's predictions, training the model to rely on less-superficial features that are more aligned with human vision, and using \"provable defenses\" that provide theoretically proven performance guarantees for the model in worst-case scenarios (https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.03824)."
